# ── Cloud AI group (server-side settings, not Zotero prefs) ──────────────
prefs-group-cloud = Cloud AI
prefs-group-cloud-desc = Stored by the littrace service as encrypted settings, not as Zotero preferences. The API key never comes back to this page.
prefs-cloud-base = API address
prefs-cloud-base-desc = The service's /v1 address, or the full /chat/completions address. HTTPS only; plain HTTP is accepted for a loopback address.
prefs-cloud-model = Model name
prefs-cloud-model-desc = The model name the endpoint expects, for example deepseek-chat.
prefs-cloud-key = API key
prefs-cloud-key-desc = Protected with Windows DPAPI by the service and never shown again. Leave it empty to keep the stored key.
prefs-cloud-proxy = Preferred local proxy
prefs-cloud-proxy-desc = Optional loopback HTTP proxy, for example http://127.0.0.1:7897. Used first; the service falls back to the system network only if the request was never sent.
prefs-cloud-budget-mode = Cost mode
prefs-cloud-budget-mode-desc = A daily limit stops work when the budget runs out and keeps the task for the next day. Unlimited keeps recording tokens but sets no ceiling.
prefs-cloud-budget-limited = Limited by a daily ceiling
prefs-cloud-budget-unlimited = No spending ceiling
prefs-cloud-daily-budget = Daily cost limit (CNY)
prefs-cloud-daily-budget-desc = Required in limited mode. Leave the other numbers blank to keep their values.
prefs-cloud-input-price = Input price (CNY per million tokens)
prefs-cloud-input-price-desc = Required in limited mode.
prefs-cloud-output-price = Output price (CNY per million tokens)
prefs-cloud-output-price-desc = Required in limited mode.
prefs-cloud-enabled = Enable cloud calls
prefs-cloud-enabled-desc = Cloud calls need an address, a model and a saved key. Cited answers and method-relation verification stay unavailable until this is on.
prefs-cloud-save = Save
prefs-cloud-test = Test connection
prefs-cloud-clear = Clear saved key
prefs-cloud-clear-hint = Clearing the key also turns cloud calls off.
prefs-cloud-loading = Reading current settings…
prefs-cloud-loaded = Current settings loaded. The key is never shown.
prefs-cloud-load-failed = Could not read the current settings ({ $detail })
prefs-cloud-saving = Saving…
prefs-cloud-saved = Settings saved. The key is never echoed back.
prefs-cloud-save-failed = Settings were not saved ({ $detail })
prefs-cloud-testing = Testing the connection…
prefs-cloud-test-failed = The connection test did not run ({ $detail })
prefs-cloud-clear-done = The saved key was cleared and cloud calls were turned off.
prefs-cloud-clear-failed = The key was not cleared ({ $detail })
prefs-cloud-key-platform-unsupported = This platform cannot protect a stored API key. Other fields save normally; see docs/support-matrix.json.
prefs-cloud-model-not-listed = The configured model is not in the endpoint's model list.
prefs-probe-detail = Service answer: { $detail }
prefs-probe-proxy-fallback = The local proxy was not used; the system network answered.
prefs-probe-ok = Reachable, and the credentials were accepted
prefs-probe-not-configured = No API address is saved yet
prefs-probe-unreachable = Could not connect to the endpoint
prefs-probe-dns = The host name did not resolve
prefs-probe-tls-certificate = The TLS certificate did not verify
prefs-probe-tls = The TLS connection broke
prefs-probe-timeout = The connection or the answer timed out
prefs-probe-auth = The credentials were rejected; check the API key
prefs-probe-redirect-refused = The endpoint asked to redirect elsewhere, which was refused
prefs-probe-unsupported = Reachable, but the endpoint serves no /models, so it cannot be verified automatically
prefs-probe-http = The endpoint answered with an error status
prefs-platform-cloud-unsupported = Cloud settings need Windows
prefs-platform-cloud-unsupported-desc = The service protects the key with Windows DPAPI, so these controls stay disabled here. See docs/support-matrix.json for the platform scope.
